# Nest layers

`apps/api` **composes**. `packages/nest` **owns domain**.

## Compose edge (`apps/api`)

`AppModule` / `GraphqlModule` wire config, global infra, `APP_FILTER`, and domain modules. No use-cases, workflows, or Drizzle there.

```ts
@Module({
  imports: [DrizzleModule, MediaModule, PubSubModule, GraphqlModule],
  providers: [{ provide: APP_FILTER, useClass: GraphqlExceptionFilter }],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

`forRoot` / `forRootAsync` (Bull, Schedule, Config, Tus) belong here. Domain modules only `registerQueue` / `forFeature`.

## Domain folders (`packages/nest/src/<domain>/`)

| Dir | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `use-cases/` | One persistence/domain verb; inline Drizzle |
| `workflows/` | Multi-step orchestration (Facade) |
| `services/` | Infra adapters (events, zip, media paths) |
| `controllers/` / `*.resolver.ts` | Transport — cookies, pipes, then workflow |
| `pipes/` | Auth/session at the edge |
| `jobs/` | BullMQ processors, cron |
| `models/` | GraphQL ObjectTypes over DB rows |
| `dto/` | GraphQL InputTypes |
| `util/` | Pure helpers (cookies, hashing, storage keys); shared Nest helpers live in `common/util` |
| `tus/` | Domain tus handler + metadata schema |

Module + primary resolver may sit at the domain root (`spaces.module.ts`, `spaces.resolver.ts`). Public export is the module (+ GraphQL models). Keep hooks/schemas internal.

## Data flow

```
resolver / controller / tus hook
  → workflow.execute
    → use-case.execute(input, tx?)
      → Drizzle
  → cookie / StreamableFile / GraphQL parent
```

GraphQL `SpacesResolver` calls **workflows only**. REST may call a workflow (unlock) plus a thin download helper; do not re-orchestrate five use-cases in the controller.

Health is a micro-domain: transport may call one composing use-case (`RunUpChecksUseCase`) instead of a `workflows/` folder.

## Secrets

Return Drizzle rows as GraphQL parents. Omit `@Field` on `authorKey`, `pinHash`, `storageKey`. Bind cookies at the edge; workflows return secrets for that (`authorKey`), they do not write cookies.

